# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
/target/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
Cargo.lock

# ...but pkcore-perf ships an executable, and a benchmark harness needs a
# pinned dependency graph: version drift silently changes the numbers it
# publishes. See the perf/ layout in
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-kernel-performance-harness-design.md.
!perf/Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk


